Z||000000||KnightRyder31||02-13-2001||10:20 PM||||How good of a car are they?<BR>Are they pretty quick?<BR>Just wondering.||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||02-13-2001||10:24 PM||||I had a 94 Grand Prix SE with the 3.1 motor in it.  I liked the car but the motor was loud and wasnt very quick.  I sold it to a friend of mine 2 years ago and last month the timing belt slipped and destroyed the motor, so if you get that car, change the belt.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||02-14-2001||11:50 AM||||Ex GF has a 90 Lumina with a 3.1. Has around 200K on it. (She bought it with 100K). I'd buy one in a heartbeat, if I was in the market for an older sedan. It's not blindingly fast, but it will get out of its own way. Exhaust has a nice rumble, too. Kinda like a GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||02-14-2001||03:43 PM||||Is it as fast as a Fiero GT?<BR>This Lumina that I'm going to buy, has only 70,000 miles, and is fully loaded and in mint cond. They want $2,500 for it. I've drivin the car, and it seems pretty quick, I didn't give it much gas to find out how fast it really was. It seems like a good deal to me, the sound system is great.<BR>Tell me what you think.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||02-14-2001||06:40 PM||||She paid $4K for hers with 100,000 miles, but you could tell it had been babied. It looked showroom. <BR>$2500 sounds reasonable. Only 70,000 miles in 9 years?! You might run a carfax check, just for giggles. Someone on the Forum had a carfax "account" available, a few weeks back. <BR>BTW... it won't be quite as fast as a GT, because it's quite a bit heavier, but it won't be a slouch, either.<BR>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000005||KnightRyder31||02-14-2001||06:57 PM||||I hope its much faster than my 2.5 Fiero!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||02-15-2001||12:24 AM||||Lumina is not as fast as the Fiero.  My friend has a 95 Lumina with the 3.1, I kill him everytime.  It's not slow, though.  Has about 130,000 miles on it and still runs nice.  The 3.1 engine is a 60* v6, just like the 2.8 in Fiero's, just stroked and the FWD version uses DIS.  Definatly not a bad car.  The "Euro" thing is just some ground effects and that wrap around wing on the trunk.<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||02-15-2001||03:10 PM||||But it is faster than a 4 cyl. Fiero, right?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GT||02-15-2001||09:30 PM||||Yeah, its quicker than the 4-Cyl fiero.  My Grand Prix was quick but not fast as it looked. It had the fancy trim around the bottom with dual exhausts much like the V6 Fieros.  ||||reg||1
